.TH PLURX-PLAYER 1 2026-10-28 "plurx-player 0.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plurx-player \- play a plurx title handed over by the plurx web app
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plurx-player
.RB [ \-\-ca
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-mpv
.IR PATH ]
.I URL
.br
.B plurx-player
.RB \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B plurx-player
handles
.B plurx-player://
links.
When Settings \(-> Playback \(-> Open titles in says plurx Player (Linux),
Play in the plurx web app opens
.IP
.B plurx-player://play?server=\c
.IB ORIGIN &code= CODE
.PP
where
.I ORIGIN
is the server's percent-encoded http(s) origin, with no path, and
.I CODE
is a one-time handoff code.
The browser starts
.B plurx-player
through its desktop entry.
It can also be run by hand with such a URL.
.PP
It redeems the code for a token scoped to one file, asks the server how to
deliver the file, plays it in the private mpv in
.IR /usr/lib/plurx-player/bin/mpv ,
and keeps the server informed until mpv closes.
The token is kept in memory only.
.PP
Any URL other than exactly
.B plurx-player://play
with
.B server
and
.B code
is refused.
.SH PLAYBACK CONTROLS
Cinema-style controls replace mpv's stock on-screen controller inside the
same video surface. Drag the full-film timeline and release to seek.
Left/Right seek ten seconds. Tab focuses controls; when the timeline has
focus, Left/Right preview and Enter commits. Escape cancels a preview or
closes a menu. Space commits a preview and toggles playback.
Controls hide after four seconds while playing, except during a preview or
an open menu, and stay visible while paused.
.PP
Audio and CC select tracks available in the current stream. Settings offers
speed and audio sync. Both Info buttons show live mpv playback diagnostics:
decoded/output picture and color, renderer/decoder, audio, FPS, packet rates,
dropped frames and demuxer estimates. Missing readings say Unavailable.
The panel refreshes only while open, including when paused. VO target
properties describe mpv's output target, not measured physical HDR output.
Library title, episode identity and synopsis come from the scoped server
context. Quality offers Auto, Original and advertised heights, preserving
position and pause; a failed replacement restores the incumbent stream.
Next resolves the immediate successor on the server. Autoplay and selected
quality are saved in playback.json under the player's config directory.
Early stream EOF offers Retry rather than marking the whole title watched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-ca " FILE"
Trust the CA certificate in
.I FILE
for a server with a private certificate.
The path is remembered for that server.
Python uses the system CA store, not the browser's.
.TP
.BI \-\-mpv " PATH"
Use this mpv binary instead of the private one.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short usage message.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/plurx-player/servers.json
The servers this user allowed.
The first time a link names a new origin, a dialog names it and the player
refuses unless the user allows it.
Plain http is allowed only through that dialog.
Any web page can open a
.B plurx-player://
link, so the list keeps a hostile page from pointing the player at its own
server.
.TP
.I ~/.config/plurx-player/mpv/
plurx Player's own mpv configuration directory, passed to mpv as
.BR \-\-config\-dir .
It does not exist by default.
.IR mpv.conf ,
.I input.conf
and scripts placed there apply to plurx Player only; the general
.I ~/.config/mpv
is never read.
mpv's built-in key bindings and on-screen controller work without it.
The options the player needs for correct output, including
.BR \-\-vo=gpu\-next ,
are on mpv's command line and take precedence over this directory.
Dolby Vision options that belong here:
.B dv\-brightness=absolute
maps for the panel's real luminance instead of the default
.BR relative ,
which follows the desktop's HDR brightness setting;
.B dv\-cm4\-trims=no
and
.B dv\-cm29\-trims=no
turn off each family's creative trims.
.PP
Both paths follow
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when it is set.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PLURX_PLAYER_MPV
The same as
.BR \-\-mpv .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The base of the configuration paths above.
.TP
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY ", " DISPLAY
When neither is set, as when the browser opens the link through
xdg\-desktop\-portal, the player takes these, with
.BR XAUTHORITY ,
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE
and
.BR XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP ,
from
.BR "systemctl \-\-user show\-environment" .
.SH NOTES
HDR output needs a Wayland compositor with wp_color_manager_v1 in HDR mode.
An accurate target luminance needs one that reports the panel's real
luminance.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1)
